# Every file in this repository is checked out exactly as it was committed.
#
# This project pins the sha256 of many files it treats as evidence: frozen
# research contracts, provider registers, acceptance records and the fixtures
# under regression/. Git on Windows rewrites line endings on checkout by
# default, which changes those bytes and therefore every one of those hashes.
#
# Measured on 2026-08-29, on a Windows runner with no .gitattributes: 23 test
# failures and 21 errors, almost all of them a checksum or a byte for byte
# comparison refusing a file that was correct when committed. The records were
# behaving properly. The checkout had altered them.
#
# Disabling the text attribute outright, rather than normalising to LF, is the
# stronger guarantee: git performs no conversion in either direction, on any
# platform, for any file, so a checkout is byte identical everywhere.
* -text
